🧠 Project Overview
This project focuses on Black-Box Optimisation (BBO), where the objective is to identify optimal input parameters for a system whose internal workings are unknown. The optimisation is performed iteratively by submitting queries and analysing the resulting outputs.
🎯 Objective
Maximise the output score of the black-box function
Identify high-performing parameter configurations
Analyse patterns in the search space to improve optimisation efficiency
📁 Dataset Description
Data Source
Generated through iterative query submissions during the BBO competition
Each data point represents one query and its resulting score
Data Structure
Each record contains:
Column Name	Description
iteration	Query number Week 1–13
function_id	Identifier for the function (1–8)
input_vector	List of input parameters
score	Output value returned by the system
strategy	Strategy used were Reinforced Learning (RL) and Gaussiona Processes (GP)
🔢 Input Features
Continuous numerical values in the range [0, 1]
Dimensionality varies depending on the function:
Function 1–2: low-dimensional
Function 6–8: higher-dimensional
📈 Data Generation Process
Initial queries generated using random sampling
Intermediate queries refined using pattern recognition and local search
Final queries generated using:
Directional updates (gradient-like)
Controlled perturbations
Exploitation of high-performing regions

⚙️ Preprocessing & Handling
Values clipped to valid range [0,1]
Inputs standardised to 6 decimal places
No missing values (fully generated dataset)
📊 Key Observations
Certain parameters had higher impact on performance
Results improved with incremental adjustments
Random exploration became less effective over time
Strong performance was found in localised regions of the search space
⚖️ Limitations
Small dataset due to limited query budget
No access to internal function behaviour
Potential noise in output scores
Limited ability to model full parameter interactions
🔁 Reproducibility
To reproduce results:
Use the provided input vectors in each iteration
Submit them to the BBO system
Record outputs and compare performance trends
